> Converted from personal notes. Amounts are for one serving. Directions are editorial, not verified source instructions.

== Ingredients ==

Gather the following ingredients: @large gluten-free corn tortillas{2} (15-small-tortilla alternative omitted as ambiguous), @shredded Monterey Jack / cheddar{3/5%cup}, @?black beans{1/5%can} (can size 15 oz; drained), @bell pepper{1/5} (diced), @onion{1/10} (diced), @olive oil{1/5%tbsp}, @cumin{1/5%tsp}, @gluten-free salsa{1/10%cup}, @sour cream{1/10%cup}, @lime{1/5}, @?cooked shredded chicken{1/5%lb}.

== Preparation ==

Soften pepper and onion in olive oil with cumin. Fill tortillas with cheese, vegetables and any chosen optional cooked filling. Cook in a skillet until crisp and the cheese melts. Serve with salsa, sour cream and lime.
